+The contract ends at the guarded invocation boundary. A command already sent downstream may outlive the installation that produced it, and physical motion cannot be rolled back. Queue fencing requires propagation of installation identity and an explicit stale-command rejection point. Controller stability, state transfer, persistent recovery, emergency-stop timing, and continual-learning quality require separate experiments. Motor-reflex adaptation after a payload shift and sensor-processing adaptation after distribution shift are two useful next task settings. Their evaluation should report task improvement and installation correctness independently: adaptation should not imply deployment.
 
